### Opt-5: REVERTED (2026-06-29)

The 2-group skip caused jit-cache=full correctness failures. Root cause:
SubqueryPreparer::MergeSubquery uses unordered_map<idx_t, unique_ptr<LogicalOperator>>
and unordered_set<idx_t> (subquery_preparer.cpp:470-471, 538-539, 569, 610).
Non-deterministic iteration order produces different expression bindings between
benchmark iterations, causing JIT cache hash collisions with mismatched types.

Error: "Failed to cast expression to type - expression type mismatch" on query
10c with jit-cache=full (12 total failures across all jit-cache=full configs).

Attempted fixes:
1. has_prior_temps_ guard: only apply 2-group skip at initial iteration (no prior
   temp tables). Passes correctness but regresses performance (+8.5% vs +4.9%).
   73 queries that hit 2-group at later iterations lose the skip.
2. Decision: fully revert. Net improvement was only 69ms (measured with 15 warm
   runs using correct parser). Not worth the complexity or DuckDB-side fix.

Files modified (revert):
- src/split/node_based_splitter.cpp: Removed 2-group skip block and
  has_prior_temps_ usage
- include/split/node_based_splitter.h: Removed has_prior_temps_ field

### Threshold Tuning (2026-06-29)

Tested thresholds: 0 (off), 200K, 500K, 1M.
Parser: plot_middleware_jit.py:analyze_middleware_breakdown() (mean of 10 warm runs).

Results (15 iterations, 113 JOB queries):
  none-split:  9684ms = 9.684s
  thresh_off: 11273ms = 11.273s (+16.4%)
  thresh_200K: 10786ms = 10.786s (+11.4%)
  thresh_500K: 10838ms = 10.838s (+11.9%)
  thresh_1M:  10631ms = 10.631s (+9.8%)

Threshold=1M is optimal: 38 winners (+789ms), 11 losers (-146ms), net +643ms.
Lower thresholds abort more aggressively but hurt more beneficial splits:
  200K: 37 winners (+1049ms), 30 losers (-559ms), net +490ms
  500K: 33 winners (+870ms), 16 losers (-439ms), net +431ms

4 queries hurt by threshold=1M (Category C: was winning, now loses):
  15c: none=91.8, off=75.5, 1M=119.0 (-43.4ms)
  15d: none=107.1, off=69.4, 1M=126.8 (-57.3ms)
  13b: none=51.7, off=51.4, 1M=55.1 (-3.7ms)
  13c: none=48.5, off=46.6, 1M=51.0 (-4.5ms)
15c/15d: iter1 produces cn JOIN mc = 1.15M standalone (triggers abort), but
subsequent iterations successfully reduce via iterative correction (iter2: 1783).
The standalone guard cannot distinguish these from 8c/9d where 1.15M compounds.

Gap attribution (Opt-1 + Opt-3, 15 warm runs):
  Threshold-aborted (28 queries):  +806ms
  2-group initial (9 queries):     +271ms (would need Opt-5 with DuckDB fix)
  Multi-iteration losers:         +1251ms (inherent split overhead)
  Winners (NB faster):            -1247ms (iterative correction strength)
  Net:                             +947ms (+9.8%)

